{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 11, :comments ["<b>Twice.</b> Because the first time it yielded only drops — for the Omnipresent had not commanded to strike it, but 'וְדִבַּרְתֶּם אֶל הַסֶּלַע' — and they spoke to a different rock and it yielded nothing. They said: perhaps it needs to be struck as the first time, as it says 'וְהִכִּיתָ בַצּוּר' (Exodus 17). That rock appeared before them and he struck it (Tanchuma)."], :book :numbers, :voice :rashi, :lang :en, :chapter 20, :notes {}, :source-witnesses nil, :timestamp "2026-08-02T09:11:43.096694397Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}